# draft
// FIRST DRAFT (M7): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
There is a second table at the end of yours this morning, with a second stamp on it, and a man in a brown robe behind it arranging his quills by length.
"Good morning. I'm the clerk." # speaker: clerk
"Of the White Christ," says Skögul, in the voice she uses for weather. # speaker: skogul
"Of his department of the dead, for the northern parishes. Such as they are." # speaker: clerk
He shows you his stamp. It says TRANSFER.
"Anyone who took the water, the baptism, is ours. You send them down the table to me, and I send them on. There is a form. I'll fill it in; you needn't trouble yourself." # speaker: clerk
"And the ones with the hammer and the cross on one cord are ours," says Skögul. # speaker: skogul
"The prime-signed. They took the sign of the cross so they could trade with us, and kept the hammer to be safe." # speaker: clerk
He sighs.
"Yes. They're yours. It's in the agreement." # speaker: clerk
"What agreement?" # speaker: skogul
"There's always an agreement." # speaker: clerk
* [Shake the clerk's hand.]
  # fx: standing clerk +1
  His hand is cool and dry, and he shakes yours exactly twice, like someone who has read how it's done.
  "I think we'll work very well together." # speaker: clerk
  Skögul eats an entire apple, core and all, without looking at either of you.
* [Stay out of it.]
  You ink your own stamps and say nothing. The clerk goes back to his quills. Skögul goes back to her apple.
- The first soul comes up the path with a small wooden cross at the neck, looks at the two tables and the two of you, and asks which queue is shorter.
-> END
